<!--
  Package validation suppressions for the SIPSorcery package.

  EnablePackageValidation in SIPSorcery.csproj makes "dotnet pack" diff the packed
  assemblies against PackageValidationBaselineVersion (the last package published to
  nuget.org) so that an accidental binary-breaking change fails the build. Every entry
  in this file is a deliberate change that was already shipped or is inherent to
  multi-targeting; each group below says which, and why it is safe to suppress.

  Adding an entry here is a decision to break binary compatibility. Do not regenerate
  this file wholesale (-p:ApiCompatGenerateSuppressionFile=true) just to get a green
  build: that silently blesses whatever the diff found and discards these comments.
  After each publish to nuget.org, bump PackageValidationBaselineVersion to the version
  just published and delete the entries the new baseline makes unnecessary.
-->
<Suppressions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">

  <!-- ==========================================================================
       Baseline validation (new package vs. the published baseline).

       The RTSP client, server, message, header and URL classes were removed as
       unmaintained in #1863 (commit 8148557). That removal is a real binary break
       for anyone who used SIPSorcery.Net.RTSP*, and it was made knowingly; these
       types are gone for good, so the break is recorded here rather than reverted.

       The removal applies to all nine target frameworks. <Left>/<Right> are omitted
       so that one entry per type covers every framework instead of nine copies.
       ========================================================================== -->
