  <!-- ==========================================================================
       Compatible-framework validation inside the package (NOT baseline-related).

       These fire between lib/net6.0/SIPSorcery.dll and lib/net8.0/SIPSorcery.dll in
       the package being built: the DTLS/SRTP code is written against Span<byte> under
       "#if NET8_0_OR_GREATER" and against ArraySegment<byte>/byte[] otherwise, so the
       two assets genuinely expose different members. These signatures already differ
       this way in every published 8.x and 10.x package; nothing in this commit changed
       them, and the types involved are low-level SRTP plumbing rather than part of the
       documented API. They are suppressed so the baseline check above is usable.

       Narrowing the split (keeping the pre-net8.0 overloads on net8.0+ as shims) is a
       library change, not a packaging one, and is left for the maintainer to judge.
       ========================================================================== -->

